.TH ares 6 "January 10, 2026"
.SH NAME
ares \- Accurate multi-system emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY ares
.B \-\-help
.YS
.SY ares
.B \-\-version
.YS
.SY ares
.B \-\-dump\-all\-settings
.YS
.SY ares
.RB [ \-\-fullscreen ]
.RB [ \-\-pseudofullscreen ]
.RB [ \-\-kiosk ]
.RB [ \-\-system \~\c
.IR system ]
.RB [ \-\-shader \~\c
.IR shader ]
.RB [ \-\-setting \~\c
.IR name=<value> ]
.RB [ \-\-no-file-prompt ]
.RB [ \-\-settings\-file \~\c
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-save\-state \~\c
.IR slot ]
.I rom
.YS

.SH DESCRIPTION

.B ares
is an emulator for systems from Atari, Nintendo, Sega, Sony, NEC, SNK,
Microsoft, Coleco, Bandai and Benesse. It is a descendent of higan and bsnes
and focuses on accuracy and preservation. The SNES emulation is especially
complete and polished.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
.br
Display a summary of options and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the version string of the application and exit
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-all\-settings
Show a list of available settings and exit
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start the emulator in fullscreen
.TP
.B \-\-pseudofullscreen
Start the emulator in pseudofullscreen mode (status bar still visible)
.TP
.B \-\-kiosk
Start in minimal UI mode (implies
.BR \-\-no-file-prompt )
.TP
.BI \-\-system " system "
Start the emulator with the given
.I system
loaded
.TP
.BI \-\-shader " shader "
Start the emulator wtih the given
.I shader
loaded
.TP
.BI \-\-setting " name=<value> "
Specify a
.I value
for the setting with the given
.I name
.TP
.B \-\-no\-file\-prompt
Do not prompt for additional optional ROMs when loading games that support it
.TP
.BI \-\-settings-file " file "
Override settings with those at the given
.IR file .
(note: if the
.I file
specified does not exist, it will be created)
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-state " slot "
Launch with the save state given by
.I slot
loaded
.TP
.I rom
.br
Full filepath of the ROM to load


.SH MORE INFO
Website:
.UR https://ares-emulator.github.io/
.UE
